    \vec{S}(x)_{R_i}.
\end{align}
Here, \(T_x\) denotes translation along the \(x\)-direction, while \(R^{\hat n}(\alpha)\) denotes a spin rotation by angle \(\alpha\) about the axis \(\hat n\). Importantly, the \(L\) and \(R\) components transform under conjugate spin-rotation representations, reflecting that the \(R\) component arises from the bra-space output of the quantum channel.

